jobs.description:
As a Logistics Employee, you will be part of a team that keeps warehouse operations running smoothly. Depending on your experience and interests, you can work in different departments.

🔧 Tools Department

In the Tools department, you work with specialized equipment and materials.

Your tasks may include:

- Checking tools and materials;
- Scanning products into the system;
- Managing stock levels;
- Preparing materials for shipment;
- Maintaining an organized workspace.

📥 Inbound Department

As an Inbound Employee, you process incoming goods and make sure everything is stored correctly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Receiving deliveries;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Scanning goods into the system;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations.

📦 Outbound Department

In Outbound, you make sure customer orders are ready to leave the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders;
- Checking products;
- Packing shipments;
- Preparing orders for transport.

🚜 Reach Truck Positions

Do you have reach truck experience or would you like to develop these skills?

As a Reach Truck Operator, you will:

- Move products throughout the warehouse;
- Replenish stock;
- Pick orders from warehouse racks;
- Work safely at height.

Don't have a certificate yet? Olympia can help you obtain one.

- You are available to work in a 2-shift schedule;
- You speak English, Dutch, or Polish;
- You are motivated and reliable;
- You enjoy working in a team;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

As an Electrotechnician, you will play a key role in ensuring the reliability and safety of electrical systems. You will work on installation projects, perform maintenance activities, and troubleshoot technical issues to keep operations running smoothly.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing electrical systems and equipment;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations to ensure compliance with safety regulations;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Collaborating with colleagues and customers to deliver high-quality solutions.

This is a varied position where no two days are the same, offering plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills.

- MBO Level 3 diploma in Electrical Engineering or a comparable technical qualification;
- Minimum of 2 years of experience as an Electrotechnician;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B is considered an advantage;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong focus on safety, quality, and precision;
- Ability to work independently as well as part of a team.

Are you detail-oriented, quality-focused, and looking for a full-time job in a dynamic logistics environment? Then this opportunity as a Quality Control Employee in Lelystad could be the perfect fit for you!

As a Quality Control Employee, you play a key role in ensuring that products meet the highest quality standards before moving further through the logistics process. You will work in a supportive team environment and be part of a 2-shift schedule (morning and afternoon shifts)

As a Quality Control Employee, your responsibilities include:

- Inspecting products to ensure they meet quality standards;
- Identifying, reporting, and helping resolve product defects;
- Carefully checking products for damages, errors, or irregularities;
- Maintaining a clean and organized work area;
- Contributing to an efficient and high-quality logistics operation;
- Following quality and safety procedures at all times.

- Basic English communication skills are required;
- Full-time availability;
- Strong attention to detail and quality;
- Ability to work effectively in a team environment;
- Ability to follow instructions accurately;
- Previous experience in quality control, production, or logistics is an advantage, but not required.

The RPH department is responsible for receiving, checking, storing and processing parts for ASML. These parts are used in high-tech machines and must be handled carefully and accurately.

Because the department covers different logistics processes, there are several opportunities available. Depending on your experience and interests, your tasks may include:

- Receiving and checking incoming goods;
- Scanning and registering products in the system;
- Picking orders;
- Moving materials within the warehouse;
- Performing stock checks;
- Packing and preparing shipments;
- Working according to quality and safety procedures.

Whether you already have warehouse experience or are looking for a new challenge, there are different roles available within the RPH department.

- Good communication skills in English;
- Availability to work full-time;
- A motivated and responsible attitude;
- Attention to detail and quality;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

As a Shipboard Electrician, you will be responsible for installing, maintaining, and troubleshooting electrical systems onboard ships and maritime installations. You will work with a variety of systems, including power distribution, lighting, navigation equipment, automation systems, and communication networks.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing and connecting electrical systems onboard vessels;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Inspecting, testing, and commissioning maritime electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical and technical faults;
- Performing maintenance and repair activities on onboard systems;
- Supporting refit, modernization, and new-build projects.

You will primarily work at shipyards, ports, and onboard vessels, with occasional travel required for project support and sea trials.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related technical field;
- Relevant experience as an electrician, preferably within shipbuilding, maritime, or offshore environments;
- Knowledge of maritime electrical systems and regulations is an advantage;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Flexible, proactive, and solution-oriented attitude;
- Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English.
